# Force LF line endings for the backup scripts (B-029), regardless of a
# checkout's core.autocrlf setting. They're bind-mounted from the host
# into a Linux (Alpine) container and run under POSIX sh — CRLF injected
# by a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true, the default here) would
# silently break them, the same class of bug as B-021 (tracked separately
# as a repo-wide fix; this entry only covers the two new files this task
# adds, not the rest of scripts/*.sh).
scripts/backup-db.sh text eol=lf
scripts/backup-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
scripts/migrate.sh text eol=lf

# Same class of fix, B-053: appliance provisioning/boot scripts, run inside
# a Debian VM via Packer (upload) and systemd (boot) -- not Windows at all.
appliance/scripts/*.sh text eol=lf

# Same class of fix, B-071: eami-proxy's entrypoint is COPYed into a Linux
# (Alpine) Docker image at build time and run as its container ENTRYPOINT
# -- a CRLF-corrupted shebang line would fail to parse on the Linux side
# exactly like the bind-mounted scripts above, just via COPY instead of a
# volume mount.
docker/caddy/docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# Same class of fix, B-072: run as the .deb/.rpm/.pkg postinstall script on
# real Linux/macOS endpoints (dpkg/rpm/macOS Installer invoke these
# directly as maintainer/postinstall scripts) -- substantially modified by
# B-072 to add real ownership/permission-bit checks on the CA-trust
# staging path, security-relevant logic that must not silently break on a
# Windows checkout. Not previously covered (a pre-existing repo-wide gap,
# same class B-021 tracks) -- added here because this brief materially
# changed these two files, not as a general fix for every script B-021
# still covers.
eami-agent/installer/linux/postinstall.sh text eol=lf
eami-agent/installer/macos/postinstall text eol=lf
